# 03 — UX Improvements

> **For the agent reading this:** Read `plans/02-basic-3d-editing` first (especially §13, Progress): it describes the editor as it exists today. This phase makes boxes fully editable with **vector-editor-style transform gizmos** (move, raise, scale, rotate), rebuilds the **tool-bar** with icons and a **contextual bar**, and ends with **multi-selection, groups and an outliner**. Every node gets a **name**, so the human and the agent can talk about "the lobby". Persistence is deliberately left for `04`. The work is split into small increments (§10). Each one ends with the human ↔ agent loop still working and a browser checklist for Orlando. `GLOSSARY.md` already has this phase's terms (marked "from 03"). As increments land, update the entries that still describe 02 behavior: hand tool, room tool / volume tool, height gizmo and selection. Log progress in a §13 at the end of this file, as 02 did.

---

## 1. Goal

One demo, end to end:

1. Orlando picks the **Box tool** (`B`). A **contextual bar** appears above the tool-bar with **Room / Volume** and the **color swatches**. He picks Volume + blue and draws a few boxes in a row. Drawing never changes the selection, so he just keeps drawing.
2. With the **Select tool** (`V`) he clicks one and drags it to a new spot, drags its **red arrow** to slide it along x only, and drags its **green arrow** to lift it until it **snaps onto the top of a room**.
3. He drags a **corner handle** to resize it (`Shift` keeps the proportions, `Alt` resizes from the center), drags the **top handle** to make it taller, and drags the **rotate handle** to turn it in 15° steps.
4. He shift-clicks two more boxes, picks yellow, and all three turn yellow. He presses `Cmd+G` and names the group **"lobby"** in the **outliner**.
5. He tells the agent *"move the lobby 6 m east and add a pillar in its center"*. The agent moves the whole group with **one** call, then draws the pillar into it. Everything shows up live, and every step is one undo.
6. He selects a box and asks *"make this twice as tall"*. The agent knows what "this" is, because it can see the selection.

