## 11. Acceptance test (end of phase)

1. `B`: the contextual bar appears. Pick Volume + blue and draw three boxes in a row. They're blue, the selection doesn't change, and the tool stays Box.
2. `V`: click a box (the gizmo appears) and drag it by its body. It follows the cursor. With `Shift` it only moves along x or z. The red and blue arrows move it along one axis.
3. Drag the green arrow up over a 3 m room: the box snaps to y = 3, standing on the wall top. `Cmd/Ctrl` lets it go anywhere.
4. Corner handle: the footprint resizes with the opposite corner fixed. `Shift` keeps the proportions and `Alt` resizes around the center. The edge handle moves one side only. The top handle changes the height.
5. Rotate handle: the box turns in 15° steps around its center. Its scale handles now resize along its rotated sides.
6. In Select, pick a room and click yellow: it turns yellow. Click Volume: it becomes solid. With two boxes selected, the kind toggle is disabled, but a color click recolors both. Switch to Box: the bar now shows the next box's style, and changing it leaves the selection alone.
   `white`, `almost-white` and `gray` are clearly distinct, on sunlit and shaded faces alike.
7. Marquee-select three boxes, `Cmd+G`, and rename the group "lobby" in the outliner. Clicking any of its boxes selects the group, and double-clicking selects the single box. Dragging moves the whole group.
8. `Delete` removes the selection, and `⌘Z` brings it back with the same IDs. Every drag and every change above is exactly one undo step, and `Esc` mid-drag cancels.
9. Agent: *"move the lobby 6 m east"* is one `move_nodes` call. *"Add a pillar in its center"* is a `draw_boxes` call with `parent` set to the lobby. Select a box and ask *"make this twice as tall"*: the agent reads `selection` and calls `update_nodes`.
10. A second tab shows the same scene and undo state. `/mcp` lists the 8 tools from §8.

